bies so that the attachment is  very strong and basically structure the  brains of men and babies in ways that  primed them towards empathy and social  relationship rather than aggression fear  and punishment I think that is an  important piece of the scientific  evidence but that alone is not going to  make it happen so we have with partners  established a or advocated towards a  early child consortium and peacebuilding  consortium and it was launched at the UN  a year ago we go back to the UN very  regularly there was the International  University of the International Year of  the family most recently there was the  United Nations General Assembly forum on  peace and so this conversation are  having are happening at the very high  level as well as in particular places in  disadvantaged neighborhoods like in in  Turkey in Brazil India share and in  Central African Republic so I think the  the global picture best there's a will  there to change things and we just need  to see the way with all the big point is  that parenting skills are not just  mothering skills that the we need to  have better means of leveraging that  father factor that we think is really  the missing ingredient the game change  in a parenting intervention would be to  bring on board the men just as strongly  as you've bought on board the women and  if I can give you another example of a  media campaign there's the he for she  campaign meaning that you don't look  after women by just advocating just  having the women advocate for themselves  engaging the men that really is the game  change or really matters so it's that  vision  and that and then putting the policies  that that don't undermine that vision  that is really important and the  excitement I think is when the science  and the policy and the practice are  coming all together and not at odds with  each other and I think that moment is  coming right I agree so that's great  well thank you very much for being here  today and sharing some of your work it's  fascinating Thank You Marilyn so we need  to make the most of fathers i believe  yes i agree i agree thank you thank you  having for more information about  professor panther brooke and her work  please visit our website at yale edu  slash McMillan report be sure to join us  again for another episode of the  McMillan report made possible through  funding from the Whitney and Betty  Macmillan Center for International and  area studies at ya  you

